/a> </li> </ul><li> <a href="#section-entry-requirements">Entry requirements</a> </li><li> <a href="#section-degree-overview">Degree overview</a> </li><li> <a href="#section-degree-structure">Degree structure</a> </li><li> <a href="#section-career-outcomes">Career outcomes</a> </li><li> <a href="#section-how-to-apply">How to apply</a> </li><li> <a href="#section-study-experience">Study experience</a> </li><ul> <li> <a href="#section-entry-requirements">Entry requirements</a> </li> <li> <a href="#section-degree-overview">Degree overview</a> </li> <li> <a href="#section-degree-structure">Degree structure</a> </li> <li> <a href="#section-career-outcomes">Career outcomes</a> </li> <li> <a href="#section-how-to-apply">How to apply</a> </li> <li> <a href="#section-study-experience">Study experience</a> </li> <li> <a href="https://adelaide.edu.au/study/enquire/">Enquire</a> <a href="https://student-adelaideuni.studylink.com">Apply</a> </li> </ul><li> <a href="#section-entry-requirements">Entry requirements</a> </li><li> <a href="#section-degree-overview">Degree overview</a> </li><li> <a href="#section-degree-structure">Degree structure</a> </li><li> <a href="#section-career-outcomes">Career outcomes</a> </li><li> <a href="#section-how-to-apply">How to apply</a> </li><li> <a href="#section-study-experience">Study experience</a> </li><li> <a href="https://adelaide.edu.au/study/enquire/">Enquire</a> <a href="https://student-adelaideuni.studylink.com">Apply</a> </li> <p><strong>Note:</strong></p> <p><a href="https://ask.adelaideuni.edu.au/app/answers/detail/a_id/4860/kw/">Additional Enrolment Information – FAQs | Adelaide University</a></p> Why Bachelor of Biomedical and Health Sciences? <p>Interested in learning how the human body works in both health and disease? Study a degree that combines biomedical sciences and health and get your career off to a healthy start. You’ll learn the basics of human disease, from its cause and diagnosis, through to novel treatments and cures.</p> <p>Be at the forefront of scientific discovery by studying a degree that is future focused and industry engaged. Develop in-demand skills that will help you play a part in addressing expected health workforce shortages.</p> Overview <p>Study the inner workings of the human body while also gaining perspectives across the broader health sector. The Bachelor of Biomedical and Health Sciences offers a sophisticated curriculum that provides knowledge and experiential learning to create major health advances.</p> <p>With a choice of eight majors, you’ll have the opportunity to tailor your studies to suit your interests and future needs. You’ll develop in-depth knowledge in your chosen disciplines and during your final year of study, you’ll participate in a research or industry placement under the supervision of qualified staff.</p> <p>You’ll graduate with relevant and transferable skills that are highly sought after in research and health industries and be able to respond to expected global health workforce shortages. Get ready for a career in the dynamic and ever-growing health sector.</p> Key features <ul><li>Study a degree with a focus on improving human health.</li><li>Choose a major to tailor your studies toward your professional goals.</li><li>Complete work or research placements in the health sector.</li><li>Access dedicated anatomy labs and study real human specimens.</li><li>Graduate with in-demand, transferable skills relevant for a variety of careers in health.</li><li>Study a degree underpinned by cutting-edge research, taught by world leading academics.</li></ul> What you''ll learn <p>The Bachelor of Biomedical and Health Sciences is an engaging and flexible three-year program that dives into human biology, health and disease. Covering the breadth of the health and medical science disciplines, it equips you with the skills and knowledge necessary to thrive in the ever-evolving health landscape.</p> <p>You''ll take core courses in health systems, research, anatomy and physiology. With an emphasis on providing cross-cultural and First Nations viewpoints, the program ensures you’ll graduate with a comprehensive and global perspective of health and care. You’ll also develop essential professional skills in communication, teamwork, problem-solving and time management. With options to select up to two majors and undertake a capstone research project, you’ll be well-prepared for a variety of diverse health-related careers.</p> <p>Throughout the program, you can broaden your expertise with elective courses or even choose to undertake a second major. One of the highlights of the Bachelor of Biomedical and Health Sciences is this flexibility, allowing you to tailor the curriculum to your interests. And there''s no rush to decide immediately – you''ll have plenty of time to explore health topics and discover what excites you.</p> Majors <p>Starting from your first year, you’ll have the option to choose up to two majors from the following areas:</p> <ul><li><a href="https://adelaideuni.edu.au/study/degrees/bachelor-of-biomedical-and-health-sciences-biochemistry">Biochemistry</a></li><li><a href="https://adelaideuni.edu.au/study/degrees/bachelor-of-biomedical-and-health-sciences-clinical-trials/">Clinical Trials</a></li><li><a href="https://adelaideuni.edu.au/study/degrees/bachelor-of-biomedical-and-health-sciences-genetics">Genetics</a></li><li><a href="https://adelaideuni.edu.au/study/degrees/bachelor-of-biomedical-and-health-sciences-medical-science/">Medical Science</a></li><li><a href="https://adelaideuni.edu.au/study/degrees/bachelor-of-biomedical-and-health-sciences-microbiology-and-immunology/">Microbiology and Immunology</a></li><li><a href="https://adelaideuni.edu.au/study/degrees/bachelor-of-biomedical-and-health-sciences-neuroscience/">Neuroscience</a></li><li><a href="https://adelaideuni.edu.au/study/degrees/bachelor-of-biomedical-and-health-sciences-public-health/">Public Health</a></li><li><a href="https://adelaideuni.edu.au/study/degrees/bachelor-of-biomedical-and-health-sciences-reproductive-and-childhood-health/">Reproductive and Childhood Health</a>.</li></ul> <p>In your final year, you''ll gain valuable and relevant real-world experience with a work placement in a professional or research setting.</p> Degree Structure: Bachelor of Biomedical and Health Sciences Program code: BBIOM <p><strong>Complete 144 units comprising:</strong></p><ul><li><strong>42</strong> units for <strong>Core courses</strong>, and</li><li><strong>48</strong> units for one <strong>Major</strong> from <strong>Majors</strong>, and</li><li><strong>6</strong> units for all <strong>Work integrated learning</strong>, and</li><li><strong>48</strong> units for <strong>Electives</strong></li></ul> Study plan <p> A study plan sets out the courses you will need to complete and the recommended timing for each one. This will help to guide your enrolment in each study period, alongside any additional information provided below. If you have received a personalised plan or alternative advice from your Program Director, please refer to that guidance in the first instance, or seek help from your Program Director or Student Assist if you are unsure. </p> Choose your course type <p> All Deselect All Common core Core courses - Program core Electives Majors Work integrated learning </p> Year 1 <h5> Semester 1</h5> Units 6 <p> <strong>HLTH1002</strong> | <a href="https://adelaide.edu.au/study/courses/hlth-1002/"> Introduction to Health Research (6 units) </a> 1 </p> Course type 1 Core courses - Program core <p> Core course </p> <p> Core courses are compulsory and build the essential knowledge for your degree. </p> Units 6 <p> <strong>HBIO1002</strong> | <a href="https://adelaide.edu.au/study/courses/hbio-1002/"> Human Anatomy and Physiology A (6 units) </a> 1 </p> Course type 1 Core courses - Program core <p> Core course </p> <p> Core courses are compulsory and build the essential knowledge for your degree. </p> Units 