-apply">How to apply</a> </li><li> <a href="#section-study-experience">Study experience</a> </li><ul> <li> <a href="#section-entry-requirements">Entry requirements</a> </li> <li> <a href="#section-degree-overview">Degree overview</a> </li> <li> <a href="#section-degree-structure">Degree structure</a> </li> <li> <a href="#section-career-outcomes">Career outcomes</a> </li> <li> <a href="#section-how-to-apply">How to apply</a> </li> <li> <a href="#section-study-experience">Study experience</a> </li> <li> <a href="https://adelaide.edu.au/study/enquire/">Enquire</a> <a href="https://student-adelaideuni.studylink.com">Apply</a> </li> </ul><li> <a href="#section-entry-requirements">Entry requirements</a> </li><li> <a href="#section-degree-overview">Degree overview</a> </li><li> <a href="#section-degree-structure">Degree structure</a> </li><li> <a href="#section-career-outcomes">Career outcomes</a> </li><li> <a href="#section-how-to-apply">How to apply</a> </li><li> <a href="#section-study-experience">Study experience</a> </li><li> <a href="https://adelaide.edu.au/study/enquire/">Enquire</a> <a href="https://student-adelaideuni.studylink.com">Apply</a> </li> <p><strong>Note:</strong></p> <p><a href="https://ask.adelaideuni.edu.au/app/answers/detail/a_id/4864">Additional Enrolment Information – FAQs | Adelaide University</a></p> Why Bachelor of Business? <p>Marketing is more than sales – it’s a science.</p> <p>Study a degree based on advanced marketing techniques and informed by industry leaders. Build the skills and knowledge necessary for a career in the marketing industry. Develop an in-depth understanding of marketing principles, consumer insights, brand development and advertising. Be equipped with core knowledge across essential disciplines of business including people management and strategic decision making. Engage in an industry internship which will enable you to explore professional pathways in sectors aligned with your interests.</p> <p>Learn from curriculum informed by industry and the world-renowned Ehrenberg Bass Institute of for Marketing Science. Graduate with the ability to understand markets, develop strategies and grow revenue for businesses. </p> Overview <p>Adelaide University’s Bachelor of Business majoring in Marketing is grounded in real-world research. You’ll master advanced marketing techniques, ensuring you graduate career ready. Courses are designed in collaboration with world-class academics and industry leaders. </p> <p>You will develop the practical skills and in-depth knowledge in areas like marketing principles, consumer insights, brand development and advertising. </p> <p>Build power skills such as resilience, curiosity and entrepreneurship to succeed in the future of business. You will be equipped with core knowledge across essential disciplines of business including accounting, people management, strategic decision making and corporate law. </p> <p>Learn to navigate dynamic global business environments and consider broad societal challenges. You will emerge as an independent learner capable of solving problems and responding with flexibility. </p> <p>Contemporary learning experiences across the degree are underpinned by industry engagement. You will have the opportunity to engage in an internship or placement and explore professional pathways in sectors aligned with your interests.</p> Key features <ul><li>Learn industry-informed marketing techniques from world-class academics. </li><li>Build power skills and core business knowledge to future-proof your career. </li><li>Gain essential enterprise knowledge to graduate career ready. </li><li>Enjoy the flexibility to study electives across different disciplines. </li><li>Discover research insights from the Ehrenberg-Bass Institute, the world’s largest centre for marketing research. </li><li>Connect with community and industry through an internship. </li></ul> What you''ll learn <p>From your first year you will focus on building a foundation of knowledge in the principles of marketing and consumer behaviour. </p> <p>Delve into advertising from the perspective of consumers, advertisers, and agencies, and examine the role of market research and analytics. Focus on brand management and develop the ability to analyse and conceptualise strategic issues to optimise business practices. </p> <p>Study core business courses including accounting, economics, people management, strategic decision making and corporate law. Build computing and programming skills to inform data-driven decision making. Your entrepreneurial mindset will be cultivated through theoretical application to build your confidence and take risks. </p> <p>Develop negotiation skills and learn to effectively collaborate, mediate and navigate workplace conflicts. Be exposed to concepts of identity, diversity, equity and inclusion to foster cross-cultural skills and explore bias and power dynamics. </p> <p>Professional placement and internship opportunities are embedded within your second and third year. Develop a practical understanding of marketing and explore career options and pathways in the context of your individual interests. </p> Majors <p>The Bachelor of Business is also available with majors in the following: </p> <ul><li><a href="https://adelaideuni.edu.au/study/degrees/bachelor-of-business-digital-business/">Digital Business</a> </li><li><a href="https://adelaideuni.edu.au/study/degrees/bachelor-of-business-human-resource-management/">Human Resource Management</a> </li><li><a href="https://adelaideuni.edu.au/study/degrees/bachelor-of-business-international-business/">International Business</a> </li><li><a href="https://adelaideuni.edu.au/study/degrees/bachelor-of-business-innovation-entrepreneurship-and-strategy/">Innovation, Entrepreneurship and Strategy</a> </li><li><a href="https://adelaideuni.edu.au/study/degrees/bachelor-of-business-management/">Management</a></li><li><a href="https://adelaideuni.edu.au/study/degrees/bachelor-of-business-marketing-and-communication/">Marketing and Communication</a></li><li><a href="https://adelaideuni.edu.au/study/degrees/bachelor-of-business-marketing-and-design/">Marketing and Design</a> </li><li><a href="https://adelaideuni.edu.au/study/degrees/bachelor-of-business-procurement-and-supply-chain-management/">Procurement and Supply Chain Management</a></li><li><a href="https://adelaideuni.edu.au/study/degrees/bachelor-of-business-project-management/">Project Management</a> </li><li><a href="https://adelaideuni.edu.au/study/degrees/bachelor-of-business-real-estate/">Real Estate</a> </li><li><a href="https://adelaideuni.edu.au/study/degrees/bachelor-of-business-sport-management/">Sport Management</a> </li><li><a href="https://adelaideuni.edu.au/study/degrees/bachelor-of-business-tourism-events-and-hospitality-management/">Tourism, Events and Hospitality Management</a>.</li></ul> Degree Structure: Bachelor of Business majoring in Marketing Program code: BBUSI <p><strong>Complete 144 units comprising:</strong></p><ul><li><strong>66</strong> to <strong>72</strong> units for <strong>Core courses</strong>, and</li><li><strong>48</strong> units for one <strong>Major</strong> from <strong>Major</strong>, and</li><li><strong>6</strong> to <strong>12</strong> units from <strong>Work integrated learning</strong>, and</li><li><strong>12</strong> to <strong>24</strong> units for <strong>Electives</strong></li></ul> Study plan <p> A study plan sets out the courses you will need to complete and the recommended timing for each one. This will help to guide your enrolment in each study period, alongside any additional information provided below. If you have received a personalised plan or alternative advice from your Program Director, please refer to that guidance in the first instance, or seek help from your Program Director or Student Assist if you are unsure. </p> Choose your course type <p> All Deselect All Common core Core courses - Program core Core courses - Program core selectives 