he program rules. </p> What courses you''ll study <p><strong>Complete 192 units comprising:</strong></p><ul><li><strong>144</strong> units for all <strong>Core courses</strong>, and</li><li><strong>6</strong> units for all <strong>Common core</strong>, and</li><li><strong>12</strong> units for <strong>Core selective</strong>, and</li><li><strong>12</strong> units for all <strong>Work integrated learning</strong>, and</li><li><strong>18</strong> units for <strong>Program electives</strong></li></ul> <p><strong>Complete 144 units for ALL of the following:</strong></p> <table> <thead> <tr> <th>Course name</th> <th>Course code</th> <th>Units</th> </tr> </thead> <tbody> <tr> <td> </td> <td> <p>Course name</p> <a href="https://adelaide.edu.au/study/courses/comp-1006/">Engineering Programming</a> </td> <td> <p>Course code</p> <p>COMP1006</p> </td> <td> <p>Units</p> <p>6</p> </td> </tr> <tr> <td> </td> <td> <p>Course name</p> <a href="https://adelaide.edu.au/study/courses/engc-1000/">Construction Materials</a> </td> <td> <p>Course code</p> <p>ENGC1000</p> </td> <td> <p>Units</p> <p>6</p> </td> </tr> <tr> <td> </td> <td> <p>Course name</p> <a href="https://adelaide.edu.au/study/courses/engc-2000/">Introduction to Water Engineering</a> </td> <td> <p>Course code</p> <p>ENGC2000</p> </td> <td> <p>Units</p> <p>6</p> </td> </tr> <tr> <td> </td> <td> <p>Course name</p> <a href="https://adelaide.edu.au/study/courses/engcx-200/">Water Treatment and Reuse Applications</a> </td> <td> <p>Course code</p> <p>ENGCX200</p> </td> <td> <p>Units</p> <p>6</p> </td> </tr> <tr> <td> </td> <td> <p>Course name</p> <a href="https://adelaide.edu.au/study/courses/engcx-301/">Hydrology and Flood Management</a> </td> <td> <p>Course code</p> <p>ENGCX301</p> </td> <td> <p>Units</p> <p>6</p> </td> </tr> <tr> <td> </td> <td> <p>Course name</p> <a href="https://adelaide.edu.au/study/courses/engi-1001/">Engineering Design and Prototyping</a> </td> <td> <p>Course code</p> <p>ENGI1001</p> </td> <td> <p>Units</