#section-degree-overview">Degree overview</a> </li><li> <a href="#section-degree-structure">Degree structure</a> </li><li> <a href="#section-career-outcomes">Career outcomes</a> </li><li> <a href="#section-how-to-apply">How to apply</a> </li><li> <a href="#section-study-experience">Study experience</a> </li><ul> <li> <a href="#section-entry-requirements">Entry requirements</a> </li> <li> <a href="#section-degree-overview">Degree overview</a> </li> <li> <a href="#section-degree-structure">Degree structure</a> </li> <li> <a href="#section-career-outcomes">Career outcomes</a> </li> <li> <a href="#section-how-to-apply">How to apply</a> </li> <li> <a href="#section-study-experience">Study experience</a> </li> <li> <a href="https://adelaide.edu.au/study/enquire/">Enquire</a> <a href="https://student-adelaideuni.studylink.com">Apply</a> </li> </ul><li> <a href="#section-entry-requirements">Entry requirements</a> </li><li> <a href="#section-degree-overview">Degree overview</a> </li><li> <a href="#section-degree-structure">Degree structure</a> </li><li> <a href="#section-career-outcomes">Career outcomes</a> </li><li> <a href="#section-how-to-apply">How to apply</a> </li><li> <a href="#section-study-experience">Study experience</a> </li><li> <a href="https://adelaide.edu.au/study/enquire/">Enquire</a> <a href="https://student-adelaideuni.studylink.com">Apply</a> </li> Why Bachelor of Mathematics (Honours)? <p>Deepen your understanding of mathematics – the foundation of current and future technologies. </p> <p>Learn to think logically and make smart decision. Gain in demand skills. Challenge yourself intellectually. Discover how mathematical theories apply to real-world problems. </p> <p>Adelaide University’s Bachelor of Mathematics (Honours) is a flexible degree that combines mathematics with complementary disciplines. Advance your analytical and research skills with an honours year, gaining valuable experience to broaden your career prospects. Prepare to tackle real-world problems as a mathematical scientist in a range of industries – from finance, healthcare and engineering to technology and academia. </p> Overview <p>The Bachelor of Mathematics (Honours) is a broad and flexible degree that can be tailored to suit your interests. You’ll build advanced knowledge in mathematics and related disciplines so you can work towards your dream career. </p> <p>You’ll tackle a range of topics in statistics, data science and applied mathematics. Learn advanced mathematical methods and theories and how to apply them to solve important industrial and social problems. Use your majors and elective courses to build your knowledge in a related discipline, preparing you to work in your desired role or industry. </p> <p>You’ll also complete an internship, supervised project or work in our dedicated Mathematics Clinic so you can get valuable industry experience. Your honours year will focus on advancing your knowledge in your chosen area of mathematics and provide you with a pathway into research or go-getting employment. </p> <p>Mathematics is a discipline that underpins all modern science, engineering, technology and most areas of academia and industry. This means you can be employed across all sectors of society, including in cutting-edge business and tech. </p> Key features <ul><li>Tailor your studies with major courses and electives in complementary areas. </li><li>Learn statistical methods of collecting and analysing data. </li><li>Get hands-on experience in our dedicated Mathematics Clinic or complete an industry internship. </li><li>Understand how mathematics underpins current and future technologies. </li><li>Complete a research-focused honours year. </li><li>Unlock a wide range of careers by pursuing high-level mathematics. </li></ul> What you''ll learn <p>This flexible degree combines essential knowledge in mathematics with disciplines of your choice, preparing you for exciting and high-impact careers. </p> <p>Your compulsory courses will expose you to topics like linear algebra, calculus, programming, research in mathematics, probability and statistics and statistical practice. You’ll also build important industry connections through our Mathematics Clinic, an internship or a supervised project. </p> <p>This degree allows you to tailor your studies with major courses and electives in complimentary areas. Major topics range from mathematical modelling, optimisation, fluid dynamics, simulation for decision science and differential equations. You might choose elective courses in survey statistics, Riemannian geometry, spatial statistics or predictive analysis. </p> <p>As part of the honours component of your degree, you’ll complete a research project in contemporary mathematics or statistics under the guidance of an academic supervisor. </p> <p>Gain essential knowledge to operate in our modern world with common core courses. Topics may include Aboriginal knowledges, ethical knowledges, artificial intelligence, cultural competency, and entrepreneurship and design thinking. </p> Majors <p>The Bachelor of Mathematics is also available with majors in the following: </p> <ul><li><a href="https://adelaideuni.edu.au/study/degrees/bachelor-of-mathematics-honours-applied-mathematics/">Applied Mathematics</a></li><li><a href="https://adelaideuni.edu.au/study/degrees/bachelor-of-mathematics-honours-data-science/">Data Science</a></li><li><a href="https://adelaideuni.edu.au/study/degrees/bachelor-of-mathematics-honours-pure-mathematics/">Pure Mathematics</a></li><li><a href="https://adelaideuni.edu.au/study/degrees/bachelor-of-mathematics-honours-statistics/">Statistics</a>.</li></ul> Design a study path that works for you <p>This degree is part of a stackable set of qualifications, meaning your study choices are flexible. If your goals shift, you can exit after one year of study with a standalone Diploma or after two years with an Associate Degree.</p> <p>You can also begin your studies with a shorter qualification like the Diploma, and continue on to complete the Associate Degree (two years) or full bachelor degree.</p> Degree Structure: Bachelor of Mathematics (Honours) Program code: HMATH <p><strong>Complete 192 units comprising:</strong></p><ul><li><strong>84</strong> units for <strong>Core courses</strong>, and</li><li><strong>18</strong> units from <strong>Work integrated learning</strong>, and</li><li><strong>Either:</strong></li><li><strong>48</strong> units for <strong>Major</strong>, or</li><li><strong>48</strong> units for <strong>Discipline courses</strong>, and</li><li><strong>42</strong> units for <strong>Electives</strong></li></ul> Study plan <p> A study plan sets out the courses you will need to complete and the recommended timing for each one. This will help to guide your enrolment in each study period, alongside any additional information provided below. If you have received a personalised plan or alternative advice from your Program Director, please refer to that guidance in the first instance, or seek help from your Program Director or Student Assist if you are unsure. </p> Choose your course type <p> All Deselect All Common core Core courses - Program core Discipline courses Discipline electives Level 2 Discipline electives Level 3 Discipline electives Level 4 Free electives Level 1 Discipline courses Level 3 Discipline courses Work integrated learning </p> Year 1 <h5> Semester 1</h5> Units 6 <p> <strong>COMP1002</strong> | <a href="https://adelaide.edu.au/study/courses/comp-1002/"> Problem Solving and Programming (6 units) </a> 1 </p> Course type 1 Core courses - Program core <p> Core course </p> <p> Core courses are compulsory and build the essential knowledge for your degree. </p> Units 6 <p> <strong>STATX100</strong> | <a href="https://adelaide.edu.au/study/courses/statx-100/"> Probability and Statistics (6 units) </a> 1 </p> Course type 1 Core courses - Program core <p> Core course </p> <p> Core courses are compulsory and build the essential knowledge for your degree. </p> Units 6 <p> <strong>MATH1004</strong> | <a href="https://adelaide.edu.au/study/courses/math-1004/"> Calculus 1 (6 units) </a> 1 </p> Course type 1 Core courses - Program core <p> Core course </p> <p> Core courses are compulsory and build the essential knowledge for your degree. </p> Units 6 <p> <a href="#level-1-discipline-courses">Level 1 Discipline courses</a> 1 </p> Course type <p> <a href="#level-1-discipline-courses"> 1 Level 1 Discipline courses </a> </p> <h5> Semester 2</h5> Units 6 <p> <strong>MATHX104</strong> | <a href="https://adelaide.edu.au/study/courses/mathx-104/"> Linear Algebra (6 units) </a> 1 </p> Course type 1 Core courses - Program core <p> Core course </p> <p> Core courses are compulsory and build the essential knowledge for your degree. </p> Units 6 <p> <strong>MATH1005</strong> | <a href="https://adelaide.edu.au/study/courses/math-1005/"> Calculus 2 (6 units) </a> 1 </p> Course type 1 Core courses - Program core <p> Core course </p> <p> Core courses are compulsory and build the essential knowledge for your degree. </p> Units 6 <p> <a href="/study/electives/">University-wide electives</a> 1 </p> Course type <p> <a href="/study/electives/">1 University-wide electives</a> </p> Units 6 <p> <a href="#common-core">Common core</a> 1 </p> Course type <a href="#common-core"> 1 Common core </a> <p> Common core </p> <p> Common core courses are interdisciplinary courses that build key graduate capabilities. </p> Year 2 <h5> Semester 1</h5> Units 6 <p> <strong>MATH1020</strong> | <a href="https://adelaide.edu.au/study/courses/math-1020/"> Communication and Research Skills in Mathematics (6 units) </a> 1 </p> Course type 1 Core courses - Program core <p> Core course </p> <p> Core courses are compulsory and build the essential knowledge for your degree. </p> Units 6 <p> <strong>MATHX203</strong> | <a href="https://adelaide.edu.au/study/courses/mathx-203/"> Multivariable Calculus (6 units) </a> 1 </p> Course type 1 Core courses - Program