cessful completion of at least 6 months full-time study (or equivalent part-time) of an <strong>undergraduate diploma</strong> (AQF level 5) or higher qualification at a recognised higher education institution.</li></ul><li>Successful completion of at least 6 months full-time study (or equivalent part-time) of an <strong>undergraduate diploma</strong> (AQF level 5) or higher qualification at a recognised higher education institution.</li><p><strong>Essential requirements - Audition</strong></p><p><strong>All applicants are required to register for an audition </strong>which involves dance, acting and singing components, as well as an interview. Selection will be based on audition score as long as academic thresholds are met.</p><p>Auditions take place in November each year in Adelaide, Melbourne, Brisbane and Perth. Auditionees are strongly encouraged to attend a live audition, but domestic and international applicants who cannot attend an in-person audition, may request to submit a recorded audition when completing your registration form. </p><p><strong>How to register for an audition</strong></p><p>1. Complete the<a href="https://able.adelaide.edu.au/music/bachelor-of-music-theatre">Bachelor of Music Theatre</a> registration audition form.</p><p>2. Pay the non-refundable audition registration fee online via <a href="https://shop.adelaide.edu.au/konakart">our online portal</a>. </p><p>3. Read the <a href="https://able.adelaide.edu.au/music/study/auditions/audition-requirements-by-program#bachelor-of-music-theatre">audition requirements </a>and prepare your material.</p><p>If you need help working out your fee or have questions about the payment process, please contact <a href="mailto:auditions@adelaide.edu.au">auditions@adelaide.edu.au</a></p> <p><b>Recognition of prior learning</b></p> <ul><li>Adelaide University is committed to recognising the contribution of students’ prior learning towards their program requirements. Credit may be granted for formal, informal, 