r your degree. </p> Units 6 <p> <strong>PSYC3018</strong> | <a href="https://adelaide.edu.au/study/courses/psyc-3018/"> Cognitive Neuroscience (6 units) </a> 1 </p> Course type 1 Core courses - Program core <p> Core course </p> <p> Core courses are compulsory and build the essential knowledge for your degree. </p> <h5> Semester 2</h5> Units 6 <p> <strong>PSYC2010</strong> | <a href="https://adelaide.edu.au/study/courses/psyc-2010/"> Psychology for Global Challenges (6 units) </a> 1 </p> Course type 1 Core courses - Program core <p> Core course </p> <p> Core courses are compulsory and build the essential knowledge for your degree. </p> Units 6 <p> <strong>PSYC2001</strong> | <a href="https://adelaide.edu.au/study/courses/psyc-2001/"> Insights into Individual Behaviour and Cognition (6 units) </a> 1 </p> Course type 1 Core courses - Program core <p> Core course </p> <p> Core courses are compulsory and build the essential knowledge for your degree. </p> Units 6 <p> <strong>PSYC2015</strong> | <a href="https://adelaide.edu.au/study/courses/psyc-2015/"> Data Science for Cognitive Neuroscience and Psychology (6 units) </a> 1 </p> Course type 1 Core courses - Program core <p> Core course </p> <p> Core courses are compulsory and build the essential knowledge for your degree. </p> Units 6 <p> <strong>PSYC2003</strong> | <a href="https://adelaide.edu.au/study/courses/psyc-2003/"> Insights into Health and Developmental Psychology (6 units) </a> 1 </p> Course type 1 Core courses - Program core <p> Core course </p> <p> Core courses are compulsory and build the essential knowledge for your degree. </p> Year 3 <h5> Semester 1</h5> Units 6 <p> <strong>PSYC3025</strong> | <a href="https://adelaide.edu.au/study/courses/psyc-3025/"> The Neuroscience of Language (6 units) </a> 1 </p> Course type 1 Core courses - Program core <p> Core course </p> <p> Core courses are compulsory and build the essential knowledge for your degree. </p> Units 6 <p> <strong>PSYC3007</strong> | <a href="https://adelaide.edu.au/study/courses/psyc-3007/"> Advanced Research Methods in Psychology (6 units) </a> 1 </p> Course type 1 Core courses - Program core <p> Core course </p> <p> Core courses are compulsory and build the essential knowledge for your degree. </p> Units 6 <p> <strong>PSYC3001</strong> | <a href="https://adelaide.edu.au/study/courses/psyc-3001/"> Advanced Individual Behaviour and Cognition (6 units) </a> 1 </p> Course type 1 Core courses - Program core <p> Core course </p> <p> Core courses are compulsory and build the essential knowledge for your degree. </p> Units 6 <p> <a href="#common-core">Common core</a> 1 </p> Course type <a href="#common-core"> 1 Common core </a> <p> Common core </p> <p> Common core courses are interdisciplinary courses that build key graduate capabilities. </p> <h5> Semester 2</h5> Units 6 <p> <strong>PSYC3011</strong> | <a href="https://adelaide.edu.au/study/courses/psyc-3011/"> Psychology for Organisations and Communities (6 units) </a> 1 </p> Course type 1 Core courses - Program core <p> Core course </p> <p> Core courses are compulsory and build the essential knowledge for your degree. </p> Units 6 <p> <strong>BIOL3024</strong> | <a href="https://adelaide.edu.au/study/courses/biol-3024/"> Neuroscience Across the Lifespan (6 units) </a> 1 </p> Course type 1 Core courses - Program core <p> Core course </p> <p> Core courses are compulsory and build the essential knowledge for your degree. </p> Units 6 <p> <strong>PSYC3003</strong> | <a href="https://adelaide.edu.au/study/courses/psyc-3003/"> Advanced Health and Developmental Psychology (6 units) </a> 1 </p> Course type 1 Core courses - Program core <p> Core course </p> <p> Core courses are compulsory and build the essential knowledge for your degree. </p> Units 6 <p> <strong>PSYC3900</strong> | <a href="https://adelaide.edu.au/study/courses/psyc-3900/"> Work Integrated Learning in Psychology (6 units) </a> 1 </p> Course type <a href="#work-integrated-learning"> 1 Work integrated learning </a> <p> Work Integrated Learning </p> <p> WIL courses give you real‑world experience as part of your degree. </p> Enrolment information <p> Find details about the rules and notes that apply to your program, along with other essential information required for successful enrolment. Supplementary supporting resources may also be provided where applicable. </p> <p>Some programs include additional enrolment advice. If available for your program, it will be displayed here.</p> <p><strong>Useful links</strong></p> <p><a href="https://adelaideuniversity.box.com/v/BPSCN-UNSBPSCN-StudyPlan-S2-26">Mid-Year Entry Study Plan</a></p> Courses <p>Listed here are all the courses that contribute to your program, including elective options that can be chosen. These courses come together to form your study plan. Courses fall into different categories, each of which have specific unit values that need to be met under the program rules. </p> What courses you''ll study <p><strong>Complete 144 units comprising:</strong></p><ul><li><strong>138</strong> units for <strong>Core courses</strong>, and</li><li><strong>6</strong> units for all <strong>Work integrated learning</strong></li></ul> <p><strong>Complete 138 units comprising:</strong></p><ul><li><strong>132</strong> units for all <strong>Program core</strong>, and</li><li><strong>6</strong> units for all <strong>Common core</strong></li></ul> <table> <thead> <tr> <th>Course name</th> <th>Course code</th> <th>Units</th> </tr> </thead> <tbody> <tr> <td> </td> <td> <p> Course name </p> <a href="https://adelaide.edu.au/study/courses/biol-3024/">Neuroscience Across the Lifespan</a> </td> <td> <p>Course code </p> <p>BIOL3024 </p> </td> <td> <p>Units </p> <p>6 </p> </td> </tr> <tr> <td> </td> <td> <p> Course name </p> <a href="https://adelaide.edu.au/study/courses/hbio-1002/">Human Anatomy and Physiology A</a> </td> <td> <p>Course code </p> <p>HBIO1002 </p> </td> <td> <p>Units </p> <p>6 </p> </td> </tr> <tr> <td> </td> <td> <p> Course n