</a> <p> Work Integrated Learning </p> <p> WIL courses give you real‑world experience as part of your degree. </p> Units 6 <p> <strong>EDUCX401</strong> | <a href="https://adelaide.edu.au/study/courses/educx-401/"> Democratic Curriculum: An Inquiry Approach (6 units) </a> 1 </p> Course type <p> <a href="#core-courses"> 1 Core courses </a> </p> Units 6 <p> <strong>EDUCX307</strong> | <a href="https://adelaide.edu.au/study/courses/educx-307/"> The Importance of Peer Relationships (6 units) </a> 1 </p> Course type <p> <a href="#core-courses"> 1 Core courses </a> </p> Enrolment information <p> Find details about the rules and notes that apply to your program, along with other essential information required for successful enrolment. Supplementary supporting resources may also be provided where applicable. </p> <p>Some programs include additional enrolment advice. If available for your program, it will be displayed here.</p> <p> <b>Notes</b> <p>Students interested in Health and Physical Education must choose both:</p><ul><li>Health and Physical Education – Health and</li><li>Health and Physical Education – Physical Education.</li></ul><p><br/></p><p>Students interested in Physics must choose Mathematics as their second discipline.</p><p><br/></p><p>Some of the disciplines have pre-requisites from Year 12.</p><ul><li>Mathematics: successful completion of SACE Stage 2 Mathematical Methods (or equivalent).</li><li>Chemistry: successful completion of SACE Stage 2 Chemistry.</li><li>Physics: successful completion of SACE Stage 2 Physics AND SACE Stage 2 Mathematical Methods.</li></ul><p><br/></p><p>It may be possible to undertake the discipline without these prerequisites, but students should consult with their Program Director first.</p><p><br/></p><p>Not all disciplines are available at all campus locations.</p><p>The following disciplines are available to Mount Gambier and Whyalla students:</p><ul><li>English</li><li>Humanities and Social Sciences - History</li><li>Digital Technologies</li><li>Psychology</li><li>TESOL. </li></ul> </p> Courses <p>Listed here are all the courses that contribute to your program, including elective options that can be chosen. These courses come together to form your study plan. Courses fall into different categories, each of which have specific unit values that need to be met under the program rules. </p> What courses you''ll study <p><strong>Complete 192 units comprising:</strong></p><ul><li><strong>60</strong> units for all <strong>Core courses</strong>, and</li><li><strong>All of the following:</strong></li><li><strong>36</strong> units for <strong>Discipline 1 courses</strong>, and</li><li><strong>36</strong> units for <strong>Discipline 2 courses</strong>, and</li><li><strong>24</strong> units for <strong>Discipline curriculum</strong>, and</li><li><strong>30</strong> units for all <strong>Work integrated learning</strong>, and</li><li><strong>6</strong> units for <strong>Electives</strong></li></ul> <p><strong>Complete 60 units for ALL of the following:</strong></p> <table> <thead> <tr> <th>Course name</th> <th>Course code</th> <th>Units</th> </tr> </thead> <tbody> <tr> <td> </td> <td> <p>Course name</p> <a href="https://adelaide.edu.au/study/courses/educ-1016/">Communicating for Equity, Agency and Engagement</a> </td> <td> <p>Course code</p> <p>EDUC1016</p> </td> <td> <p>Units</p> <p>6</p> </td> </tr> <tr> <td> </td> <td> <p>Course name</p> <a href="https://adelaide.edu.au/study/courses/educ-1119/">Classroom Management in Secondary Contexts</a> </td> <td> <p>Course code</p> <p>EDUC1119</p> </td> <td> <p>Units</p> <p>6</p> </td> </tr> <tr> <td> </td> <td> <p>Course name</p> <a href="https://adelaide.edu.au/study/courses/educ-6112/">Inclusive Education and Responsive Teaching in Secondary Contexts</a> </td> <td> <p>Course code</p> <p>EDUC6112</p> </td> <td> <p>Units</p> <p>6</p> </td> </tr> <tr> <td> </td> <td> <p>Course name</p> <a href="https://adelaide.edu.au/study/courses/educx-103/">Effective Pe