ants must submit a CV and a 60-second visual effects showreel.</li></ul><li>A completed <strong>bachelor</strong> degree (AQF level 7) or higher from a recognised higher education institution; OR</li><li>A completed <strong>Advanced Diploma</strong> (AQF level 6) from a registered training organisation (RTO); OR</li><li>Three years'' experience in the visual effects industry or the creative industries with a relevant showreel of visual effects work.</li><li>All applicants must submit a CV and a 60-second visual effects showreel.</li> <p><b>Recognition of prior learning</b></p> <ul><li>Adelaide University is committed to recognising the contribution of students’ prior learning towards their program requirements. Credit may be granted for formal, informal, and non-formal learning. Visit the <a href="https://adelaide.edu.au/study/how-to-apply/entry-pathways/credit/">Credit for previous study</a> page for more information.</li><li>Answer a few simple questions with our online <a href="https://apps.adelaide.edu.au/public/creditassessor/">Credit Assessor</a> to see what credit you could get.</li></ul> <p><b>Recognition of prior learning</b></p><ul><li>Adelaide University is committed to recognising the contribution of students’ prior learning towards their program requirements. Credit may be granted for formal, informal, and non-formal learning. Visit the <a href="https://adelaide.edu.au/study/how-to-apply/entry-pathways/credit/">Credit for previous study</a> page for more information.</li><li>Answer a few simple questions with our online <a href="https://apps.adelaide.edu.au/public/creditassessor/">Credit Assessor</a> to see what credit you could get.</li></ul><li>Adelaide University is committed to recognising the contribution of students’ prior learning towards their program requirements. Credit may be granted for formal, informal, and non-formal learning. Visit the <a href="https://adelaide.edu.au/study/how-to-apply/entry-pathways/credit/">Credit for previous study</a