UPDATE courses SET
    course_description = '<h4>Overview</h4><p>This graduate certificate will provide you with the foundational, practical and theoretical counselling knowledge to support Australia’s mental health workforce. </p><p>Your studies will cover topics across fundamental counselling skills, counselling and psychotherapy theory, ethics, attachment processes and qualitative research methods in health. Tailor your studies to suit your interests with elective courses and have opportunities to practice your skills with partner work. By the end of your six months of study, you might choose to continue your studies with our graduate diploma or master program. </p> Key features <ul><li>Learn from experienced counsellors. </li><li>Explore topics covering ethics, attachment and research in counselling and psychotherapy. </li><li>Establish practical counselling skills. </li><li>Practice and deepen your skills with case studies. </li><li>Select elective courses aligned to your interests. </li><li>Enjoy the option to continue your studies with a graduate diploma or master.</li></ul>  ',
