UPDATE courses SET
    course_description = '<h4>Overview</h4><p>Our Master of Public Health offers a two-year path to a career in the health sector, where you can make a real impact every day. </p><p>Explore key areas like epidemiology, health promotion, biostatistics, communicable diseases and global public health. Connect with leading academics, researchers and policy makers who will mentor you and guide your studies. </p><p>Choose a study pathway that aligns with your ambitions and interests – whether it’s a research dissertation, thesis or practical industry placement. </p><p>You’ll graduate from Adelaide University with the skills to influence public health policy, advocate for change, and improve the wellbeing of entire communities. Create a deeply rewarding career, working in a non-clinical setting and collaborating with other health professionals to contribute to a healthier, safer, and more equitable society. </p> Key features <ul><li>Build expertise in public health practice and policy. </li><li>Engage with mentors, active researchers, practitioners and policy makers. </li><li>Develop advanced problem-solving and research skills. </li><li>Gain practical experience and network with public health leaders through industry placements. </li><li>Advance your career in a field with very strong projected employment growth. </li><li>Tailor your studies to your future ambitions, with pathways in research or professional placements.</li></ul>  ',
    course_duration_per_week = 104,
    offshore_tuition_fee = 101000,
    onshore_tuition_fee = NULL,
    enrolment_fee = 150,
    materials_fee = NULL,
